<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Stocks stay quiet.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Stocks stay quiet.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks were quiet in after-hours trading, traders said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There's nothing that jumps out at me,&quot; said one trader.  </p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one had a volume of 12,200 shares against Monday's 39,600, while session two had 183,400, compared to 151,600.</p>
